DeviceCreationDesc: "vkInstanceCreateInfoNext", a caller's chain for "VkInstanceCreateInfo::pNext".

NRI creates the Vulkan instance itself, and the only structures it chains into
VkInstanceCreateInfo are its own (VkDebugUtilsMessengerCreateInfoEXT, and VkValidationFeaturesEXT
with "enableGraphicsAPIValidation"). So a caller cannot pass VkLayerSettingsCreateInfoEXT
(VK_EXT_layer_settings) and has to configure the Khronos layer through environment variables or
vk_layer_settings.txt, which apply to every instance in the process, are read from the process
environment at instance creation (a managed host on Linux or macOS does not update it), and cannot
differ between two devices.

This adds "vkInstanceCreateInfoNext" next to "vkExtensions": a caller's pNext chain, appended after
NRI's own structures (the chain is the caller's and stays const, so it goes last). Ignored by the
wrapper path, whose instance is the caller's, and by the other backends. Measured on NRI main
72f5f46, NVIDIA, layer 1.4.341: a VkLayerSettingsCreateInfoEXT setting "validate_best_practices"
switches the best-practices checks on for that device only.

